  "name": "Test AI video hooks as Instagram trial reels with Gemini, Veo 3.1 and PostWire",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "6c54587d-fabd-4fdb-af5b-65e603b6a363",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -650,
        -97
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 520,
        "height": 762,
        "content": "## Test video hooks as Instagram trial reels\nType one video idea in a form and test two or three opening hooks. Gemini writes the hooks, Veo 3.1 renders a clip for each, and PostWire publishes every clip as an Instagram trial reel.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Hook test brief** is an n8n form: the video idea, the audience and how many variants to test.\n2. **Write the hooks with Gemini** returns one hook, Veo prompt and caption per variant: the same idea opened in different ways.\n3. For each variant, **Generate the variant with Veo 3.1** renders 8 seconds in 9:16 and the file goes straight to a PostWire upload slot.\n4. **Publish as a trial reel** posts each clip as a trial reel, which Instagram shows to non-followers first and shares with your followers only if it performs. Accounts without trial reels get a normal Reel.\n5. Every variant is logged in Google Sheets with its hook and result; when Instagram refuses one, **Gmail** emails you the fix.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create a free account at postwire.io, connect your networks and copy your API key. In n8n add a **Header Auth** credential (name `Authorization`, value `Bearer pw_live_\u2026`) and select it in the three PostWire nodes. Connect an Instagram professional account.\n2. Add a Google Gemini credential with billing enabled (about one dollar per variant with Veo 3.1 Fast).\n3. Create a sheet with the columns date, idea, variant, hook, status, link and note, and pick it in both Sheets nodes.\n4. Connect Gmail and put your address in **Email me the fix**, then open the form URL from **Hook test brief**.\n\n### Customize\nChange the hook styles in the Gemini system message, or the number of variants in the form."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
